{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% import "_stream.njk" as s %}

{#
  Latest -- the page she lands on.

  ONE TIME AXIS, read downwards. `future` is what is coming: the open tasks'
  due dates in day groups, furthest away at the top, everything late in one
  "Overdue" group at the bottom of the block. Then the Today line, which always
  exists (empty on a quiet day) and carries the `#today` anchor the toggle and
  the login redirect both point at -- and directly under it the twisty holding
  the open tasks that have no due date at all, which are not later, they are
  open now. Then `days`: what has happened, newest first, files and task
  changes interleaved by time alone.

  So: scroll up for the future, scroll down for the past, and she arrives on
  the line between them -- the `#today` anchor alone gets her there whenever the
  URL carries it, with scripting on or off. public/stream.js, loaded at the
  bottom of this file, is for the one URL that cannot: plain `/`, from a
  bookmark or a home-screen icon.
#}

{% block heading %}
  {% if viewer %}Hello, {{ viewer.label }}{% else %}Latest{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  {#
    When she was last here, and what the badges mean -- in that order, because
    the second only makes sense once she knows there was a "last time". Absent
    on a first-ever visit: nothing is badged then, and there is no previous
    sitting to name.
  #}
  {% if lastVisitedAt %}
    <p class="section__note">
      You were last here {{ lastVisitedAt }}.{% if newCount %} Newer things are marked New.{% endif %}
    </p>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="stream" aria-labelledby="stream-heading">
    <h2 class="section__title visually-hidden" id="stream-heading">What is coming, and what has changed</h2>

    {#
      Above the line. The cap is implausible for a household (see
      `moreUpcomingLabel` in src/lib/stream.js) -- but when it bites, the rows
      that were dropped are the furthest away, so the note goes at the top of
      the block where they would have been.
    #}
    {% if moreUpcomingLabel %}
      <p class="section__more">{{ moreUpcomingLabel }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% for group in future %}
      {{ s.due_group(group) }}
    {% endfor %}

    {#
      The files are all here; the tasks may not be. Said quietly, and above the
      history so it is read before the rows it is a caveat about -- never as an
      error page, because the page she asked for is right here.
    #}
    {% if tasksUnavailable %}
      <p class="section__note section__note--quiet">Tasks couldn’t be checked just now.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {#
      The undated twisty is handed to every day group and rendered by exactly
      one of them -- Today's, directly under the heading, before the day's rows
      and before the "Nothing has changed yet" line below. It is not on the
      axis, so it is not laid out along it; it is part of the state of today,
      and today is where the page lands. `undated_twisty` in _stream.njk has
      the reasoning.
    #}
    {% for day in days %}
      {{ s.day_group(day, undated) }}
    {% endfor %}

    {#
      Only shown when there is genuinely nothing: the day groups above always
      include today, so this sits under a bare "Today" heading. A claim we can
      finally make honestly -- it is no longer the same rendering as "the lookup
      failed", because a failed lookup now reaches the error pages instead.

      `moreLabel` is the one thing that takes it back off the page: a walk that
      gave up at its bounds and found nothing cannot say nothing has changed,
      only that it did not look everywhere. That case shows the line below and
      this one not at all.
    #}
    {% if total == 0 and not moreLabel %}
      <p class="empty">Nothing has changed yet.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {#
      The page is a window on the history, not the whole of it. Said whenever
      the fetch came back full or the fallback walk gave up early -- see
      `moreLabel` in src/lib/stream.js.
    #}
    {% if moreLabel %}
      <p class="section__more">{{ moreLabel }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
{% endblock %}

{#
  Landing on Today when the URL has no fragment to land on -- a bookmark, a
  home-screen icon, a typed address. Progressive enhancement only: every link
  into this page still carries `/#today`, and with JavaScript off the anchor is
  the whole mechanism, exactly as it was.
#}
{% block scripts %}
  <script src="/public/stream.js?v={{ appVersion }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
